Z||000000||kornholio||03-27-2000||10:47 PM||||Just wondering...if the fuel injectors on my V6 are leaking, approximately how much would it cost to replace them (parts and labour)?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Linx||03-28-2000||09:41 AM||||$30 per injector at Advance Auto Parts.  $51 at Autozone.  If you're just needing the o-rings...$8 for all of them.  Adds up quick, dont it?<P>As for labor, replacing 'em is easy.  Why would you want to pay anyone?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Linx (edited 03-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||kornholio||03-28-2000||06:44 PM||||ok.  Next question:  What's involved in replacing the fuel injectors?  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||03-28-2000||06:49 PM||||Friends,<P>I believe that I am experiencing a leaking injector.  Does anyone know how to differentiate if the o-ring is the cause of the leak or it is the injector itself?  The car in question is a 68K 85 GT.<P>Many Thanks,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||5
Z||000004||AL||03-28-2000||10:03 PM||||first you take the fuel fuse out, start car till it dies,then take The plenum off and everything you see around it, after that go to the firewall next to the battery, dissconnect the fuel lines from there,then you will see, the fuel rail take the two bolts that are in the fuse block,remove the block, then you will see two more screws holding the rail, take those out and pull the rail out, then you will see little locks on top of every injector, move them to the right and pull out the injector and do that to the one's you are going to change. once you put in all the new injectors in put oil or wd40 on the o rings and put in the fuel rail back in it's place,and since you have it all apart check the vacuam lines to see if none are broken, if they are buy some regular vacuam hoses and install them instead of the plastic lines that leak and break easy,also the reason i'm telling you to disconect the lines  of the fuel by the battery is that if you disconnect them at the fuel block you might strip the block when you install the lines there, so better for you to disconnect the lines  by the battery.good luck. to check if the injector is leaking you have to measure the pressure on that injector, if it's low compared to the rest of the injectors then it's the injector that is bad, if it shows the same as the other injectors then it's a o ring, good luck guys,AL. ||||reg||14
